    TEST-0001: design the tests the core's unit tests can't replace
    
    The unit tests in test/core/rooms.spec.ts cover the business logic with
    plain objects and a fake store. Anything that goes wrong outside the
    core gets past them, so each pending test here names something only a
    wider test can see, at the narrowest level that can see it.
    
    Integration, a real JsonBookingStore on a real file and no core:
    - a new store, before its file exists
    - reading back what was written, which translates startTime into start
    - the field names in the file, which Facilities' tools depend on. A
      store that wrote start instead of startTime could still read its own
      bookings back, so this one has to read the file directly.
    
    End to end, run() with the real core and a real store: main.ts reads
    argv, calls the core, and words the answer. Only a test through run()
    can see that wiring. One test covers it, because the business logic
    and the file are covered below.

